#: 7d91b7619ff8416e89f399a3ce4e35e1
msgid "Linear algebra API"
msgstr "线性代数 API"

#: 23ded40a738040979846dd8ab99d3b24
msgid ""
"The `jittor.linalg` module covers matrix decompositions, linear solves, "
"eigenvalue routines, norms, and Einstein summation."
msgstr ""

#: 0abacedb61684738856a9a0b0a54382a
msgid ""
"do Cholesky decomposition of x in the form of below formula: x = LL^T x "
"must be a Hermite and positive-definite matrix. L is a lower-triangular "
"matrix. :param x (...,M,M): :return: L (...,M,M)."
msgstr ""

#: ddbaf347f7734e36909c618755179330
msgid ""
"calculate the determinant of x. :param x (...,M,M): :return:\\|x\\| "
"(...,1)"
msgstr ""

#: 9005a3635ab440da986dcd5da45a66c6
msgid ""
"calculate the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of x. :param x (...,M,M): "
":return:w, v. w (...,M) : the eigenvalues. v (...,M,M) : normalized "
"eigenvectors."
msgstr ""

#: ad73a1e820944405bd0b906fe07dfc69
msgid "Evaluate the Einstein summation convention on the operands."
msgstr ""

#: 23371aff9bb94818a5cb81e8eae44b3f
msgid ""
"Native jittor implementation: GEMM-shaped contractions dispatch to "
"``jt.matmul`` (cublas on GPU). Other cases are expressed with the "
"existing jittor tensor ops used by this implementation, including "
"``reindex`` for diagonal handling, element-wise operations, reductions "
"such as ``sum``, and reshapes/transposes as needed. No numpy round-trip, "
"so ``float16`` and ``bfloat16`` operands stay on-device throughout and "
"autograd is provided by the underlying jittor ops."
msgstr ""

#: bc2dd7ccf921461a83f16f6199c4c844
msgid "calculate the inverse of x. :param x (...,M,M): :return:x^-1 (...,M,M)."
msgstr ""

#: 3bb6766693df4b59bcfe5cb89c17460c
msgid "General ``torch.linalg.norm`` / ``numpy.linalg.norm`` dispatcher."
msgstr ""

#: 014bb55fc6e848b4b74e362d008f60b5
msgid "Behaviour (matching torch/numpy):"
msgstr ""

#: 03271485d4a541c4bc0478138c7ddad7
msgid ""
"``dim`` is a 2-tuple, or ``dim is None`` and ``x`` is 2-D: matrix norm "
"(default ``ord`` is the Frobenius norm), see :func:`matrix_norm`."
msgstr ""

#: c9d148f0df344750a85c552566de90e0
msgid ""
"``dim`` is an int, or ``dim is None`` and ``x`` is 1-D, or ``ord`` is set"
" with ``dim is None``: vector norm (default ``ord`` is 2), see "
":func:`vector_norm`."
msgstr ""

#: 7fb0d24e88954197b2ca0c07f1674d01
msgid ""
"``dim is None`` and ``ord is None``: the 2-norm of the flattened tensor "
"(Frobenius), built from native jittor ops."
msgstr ""

#: 35735489fd1443079b642e30d3e6acda a3a9c37e9bf04191a8e6c4130d7e70b4
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: d0a59d0fbf9743afb1506a3105702f08
msgid "input tensor."
msgstr ""

#: f03b170aa9a94d868b970f58cf33261a
msgid ""
"order of the norm; meaning depends on whether a matrix or a vector norm "
"is selected (see :func:`matrix_norm` / :func:`vector_norm`)."
msgstr ""

#: 8a2d16fbd60e4bb3b51755ab6d787885
msgid "axis/axes defining the norm."
msgstr ""

#: fdaf8845f669456b8abc29916948a7bd
msgid "keep reduced dims as size-1."
msgstr ""

#: 1d7f3a1312be488ca41b3ace9d7337ca 78f8ebd530e34812bf0346d97e651e7a
msgid "Returns"
msgstr ""

#: 70ff5e1976c94cffb85b4a06cf1ef50c
msgid "the requested norm."
msgstr ""

#: 348760b20432406ca8c0615c134d1a08
msgid ""
"calculate the pseudo-inverse of a x. :param x (...,M,N) :return: x's pinv"
" (...N,M)"
msgstr ""

#: c8d039aaefd04a61b53c52578393b0dc
msgid ""
"do the qr factorization of x in the below formula: x = QR where Q is "
"orthogonal matrix and R is upper-triangle matrix. :param x (...,M,M): "
":return:q,r as the result of qr factorization.They are both in the shape "
"of (...,M,M)."
msgstr ""

#: ae0cd86179e74dbca934bd3d3852c6c4
msgid ""
"calculate the sign and log of the determinant of x. :param x (...,M,M): "
":return sign, x's logdet. sign array decides the sign of determinant and "
"their values can be -1,0,1.Only Real number now.0 means det is 0 and "
"logdet is -inf. logdet in shape (...,1)."
msgstr ""

#: 426687c6501041b28a9098dda3a5a2ed
msgid ""
"Solve a linear matrix equation Ax = B.This is done by calculating x = "
"A^-1B.So A must not be singular. :param a:(...,M,M) :param b:(...,M) "
":return:solution of Ax = b formula.x in the shape of (...M)"
msgstr ""

#: c3c79bcbb0a5412f85a0f49573a77601
msgid ""
"Singular Value Decomposition: ``A = U @ diag(S) @ Vh``. Returns the same "
"named ``(U, S, Vh)`` result as ``torch.linalg.svd`` (and it also unpacks "
"as a plain 3-tuple ``u, s, v``, preserving every existing jittor caller)."
msgstr ""

#: 12a89d06ebd64cbfba58885174412040
msgid "For ``A`` of shape ``(...,M,N)`` with ``K = min(M, N)``:"
msgstr ""

#: fd0a9d6a0e7c46fe9c0e0fe4f4661dbb
msgid ""
"``full_matrices=False`` (default, reduced / \"thin\"): ``U`` is "
"``(...,M,K)``, ``Vh`` is ``(...,K,N)``, ``S`` is ``(...,K)``."
msgstr ""

#: 668c4e8571c244c0a056944167bcb49a
msgid ""
"``full_matrices=True``: ``U`` is ``(...,M,M)``, ``Vh`` is ``(...,N,N)``, "
"``S`` is ``(...,K)``."
msgstr ""

#: 466d25186e4b43c0b5402a8b82b0836f
msgid ""
"``torch.linalg.svd`` defaults to ``full_matrices=True``; this jittor- "
"native entry point keeps the historical reduced default so that the "
"differentiable path and all jittor callers (``matrix_rank``/``cond``/ "
"``matrix_norm``/the native ``test_linalg`` suite) are unchanged. Pass "
"``full_matrices=True`` explicitly for torch's full shapes. (The torch- "
"facing ``torch.linalg.svd`` default is meant to be supplied at the torch-"
"compat boundary.)"
msgstr ""

#: 99da9000ddea476694fe4e23601a16ee
msgid ""
"``S`` is sorted in descending order. The reduced form (and the square "
"case, where reduced == full) is differentiable; the full form on a *non-"
"square* matrix is computed via numpy without a gradient on ``U``/``Vh`` "
"(the extra orthogonal-complement columns/rows have no unique gradient) — "
"use ``full_matrices=False`` or :func:`svdvals` when gradients are needed."
msgstr ""

#: 710512a11e65431eb728f4e6c70cf888
msgid "``(...,M,N)`` real matrix (or ``nn.ComplexNumber``)."
msgstr ""

#: 654ba7e6e0bf4762aeda6c850226363c
msgid "see above. Default ``False`` (reduced)."
msgstr ""

#: b415ed0e2ce347759daacf38530110c1
msgid ""
"if ``False``, only ``S`` is meaningful (``U`` and ``Vh`` are still "
"returned for shape compatibility but may be skipped)."
msgstr ""

#: ea4f75ab8c424a6eb1b7d1ed11a9c539
msgid "accepted for torch signature compatibility (ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: 40d67addc6b240c2adf8ae099ebedd79
msgid "named tuple ``SVD(U, S, Vh)``."
msgstr ""
